# Netlify _headers — SOMA KeyDrop v0 (Locke F3, 2026-08-14).
#
# This page holds a live secret (rk_live_... Stripe key) in a DOM password
# field. The load-bearing line is connect-src: even if a script on this page
# were compromised (injected or supply-chain), it cannot fetch/XHR/beacon
# anywhere except our own origin, SOMA Auth, and the estate feedback service —
# nowhere an attacker-controlled endpoint could receive the exfiltrated value.
#
# script-src has NO 'unsafe-inline' — index.html/login.html's inline <script>
# blocks were extracted to /js/app.js and /js/login-app.js specifically so
# this could be tight (an injected inline script literally cannot execute).
# supabase-js is vendored locally (/vendor/supabase-js/) rather than loaded
# from jsdelivr, so no third-party script origin is needed at all.
#
# style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' (the page's CSS lives in <style> blocks in
# <head>; low residual risk — style injection can't exfiltrate a password
# field's value the way script injection can, and the connect-src restriction
# neuters that vector regardless of source).
#
# https://vpsmikewolf.duckdns.org is the estate feedback-chip service
# (vendor/soma-feedback/soma-feedback.js, required standard on every SOMA
# site). Google One Tap is disabled site-wide via data-no-google on both
# pages, so accounts.google.com is never contacted and is deliberately not
# allow-listed here.

